<title>USA: N.Y. business loans rose $1.02 bln in March 5 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans rose $1.02 bln in March 5 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $1.020 billion to $45,745 billion in the week ended March 5, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $1.009 billion to $45,998 billion.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $2.790 billion to $817,115 billion.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
</text>
